  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 removes any sales stop for models above 5% (exceeding the limit only triggers corrective action and regulator-discretionary restrictions), which is the rule most favourable to Northwind's Hearth 10. S5 keeps a mandatory 8-per-100k recall with no transition, which is costly for Halcyon's Ember 8 but does not bar sales, while S3 sets a 72-month retrofit deadline that favours Northwind's low shut-off coverage."
